# Contributions. One row per thing somebody wants to add: a person, a society, a place,
# an event, or a connection between two of them. Fill in the template CSV
# (contribute-template.csv in the repository root), save it as pipe-delimited, and paste
# the rows in below the line; or send the CSV to whoever runs the build and they will.
#
# Everything here is kept separate from the transcription of the source, and everything
# added this way is marked on the page as contributed and needing checking, with the
# contributor's name against it, until somebody confirms it.
#
# WHAT GOES IN EACH COLUMN
#   what        person | society | place | event | connection
#   name        the person, society, place or event. For a connection, leave blank.
#   from / to   for a connection only: the two things it joins, by name or by reference.
#               Both must already exist here, or be added on their own rows first.
#   how         for a connection only: one of the connection types (see
#               src/connection-types.psv), or plain words and we will match it.
#   field       nat | press | trade | suff | reform | civic | arts  (see the rail)
#   dates       1826-1894, or 1850s, or 1857. Anything we can read a decade out of.
#   what_they_did  a sentence or two a stranger could read. This is what the page shows.
#   where       a district, a street, or lat,lon if you have it
#   sure        yes = you have a source | no = you are fairly confident | reading = an argument
#   source      a URL, a shelfmark, a book and page. Something somebody else could check.
#   by          your name, so the entry can be attributed and queried
#   notes       anything the columns above have no room for
#
# what|name|from|to|how|field|dates|what_they_did|where|sure|source|by|notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (no contributions yet)
